# Data / research artifacts (large, regenerable, or external-drive-backed).
# Nothing under data/ is tracked, including data/metadata/'s WRDS pull
# manifests and library-list file (tried once, reverted -- see git
# history). Those aren't static provenance: append_manifest_row() appends
# to the manifests on every pull, and pull_wrds_reference.py rewrites
# wrds_available_libraries.txt wholesale. last_manifest_fingerprint_for_path()
# reads the manifest back to decide whether a chunk gets re-pulled, so a
# git-tracked copy makes `git merge`/checkout a destructive writer of live
# run state: a local untracked copy gets silently overwritten with no
# conflict, and worse, these paths are symlinked to a shared location from
# every agent worktree, so a merge that brings a tracked file under a
# symlinked directory deletes the symlink outright, disconnecting that
# worktree from all of data/metadata/. A `merge=union` driver doesn't help
# either -- both failure modes are one-sided adds over an ignored/symlinked
# path, so no merge driver ever runs. The same reasoning applies to any
# other file under data/ (e.g. a slice's FINDINGS.md) -- no exceptions, no
# matter how static a given file looks today: put durable, reviewable
# write-ups in reports/ instead, which has no symlink-sharing hazard.
/data/
mlruns/
experiments/
outputs/
*.parquet
*.duckdb

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Claude Code agent tooling: only the isolated git worktrees created for
# background subagents and machine-local settings overrides are scratch
# state -- project-scoped config (settings.json, agents/, commands/,
# hooks/, skills/) is deliberately left trackable.
/.claude/worktrees/
/.claude/settings.local.json
